+## Durations
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a string into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. It accepts either a whole number of
+seconds (`120`) or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d`, `h`, `m` and `s`, each at most once and
+in that order, with no spaces, case-insensitively. For example `2d`, `1h30m`, `45S` and `1d2h3m4s`. Anything else, such
+as `1.5h`, `-5` or `30m1h`, is rejected.
+
+```python
+@click.command()
+@click.option("--wait", type=click.Duration())
+def cli(wait):
+    click.echo(repr(wait))  # "1h30m" -> datetime.timedelta(seconds=5400)
+```
+
